  "notes": "Waiver filing (Exhibit A), cash basis, period 10/1/21-9/30/22. Page 1 / page 2 TOTAL columns include pages 1a / 2a. Governmental = General, Street, Fire Hall, Community Redevelopment, ARPA; business-type = Utility, Sewer O/M, Water Deposit, Sewer Reserve, Water Reserve (same split as FY2023/FY2024). Mixed Local Receipts: Other row split by fund column (split_from); other statement lines are single-fund-type rows taken from the TOTAL column. Cash fields are the line 3 / line 28 subtotals (net cash + investments); investments shown separately for information. Transfers: line 20 'Transfers In Other Than Surplus Fees' 95,184.94 (General 51,115.00, ARPA 44,069.94) and line 49 'Transfers Out of Surplus Fees' 95,184.94 (General 22,034.97, Street 25,557.50, Utility 12,778.75, Sewer O/M 34,813.72); the Schedule of Interfund Transfers p5 totals 95,184.94 but attributes 34,813.72 to the Utility Fund and 12,778.75 to the Sewer Fund (Exhibit A columns show the reverse); recorded as Exhibit A prints. transfers_in is the printed Total-column figure; transfers_out is the governmental share of line 49. 'Other Capital Outlay' printed only in the Street Fund column, labelled Capital Outlay: Streets/Highways. Debt Service 20,659.12 is in the Utility Fund column (business-type). Schedule of Outstanding Debt p5: Water Loan 289,433.14 outstanding (not on the cash-basis balance sheet). Governmental identity: 201,130.91 + 295,236.49 - 268,553.83 + 95,184.94 - 47,592.47 = 275,406.04. Business-type: 307,075.01 + 110,455.29 - 67,691.78 - 47,592.47 = 302,246.05. County Treasurer balances 1,733.62 (10/1/21) and 1,265.03 (9/30/22) informational. Read pages 1-5 of 5"
